# SPEC: 44_8_prefab_static,44_8_vocab
# Negative test (Tier 2, child-known): v.set_text("<child>", …) with a
# child name that is NOT declared in the `children:` list of the prefab
# from which v was instantiated.  At runtime → find_child NULL → silent no-op;
# so it must be a HARD compiler error.  See spec/44_8.
#
# Expected exit code: 1
#
# Diagnostic form:
#   ...: 'inst'.set_text("does_not_exist") addresses an unknown child of prefab
#   'Panel' — no child with that name is declared in its `children:` list. ...

- prefab:
    name: Panel
    width: 100
    height: 40
    children:
      - { name: title, type: label, x: 0, y: 0, width: 100, height: 20 }

- def:
    name: main
    return: i32
    body:
      - decl: [inst, prefab_instance, { call: [engine.instantiate, "Panel"] }]
      - call: [inst.set_text, "does_not_exist", "hi"]
      - return: 0
